// C round-trip for the substr bounds (DEC-018): astra_builtin_substr must
// word a negative start exactly like the seed VM — the length overrun and the
// start > len(s) cases live in conformance/expressions/, which sweep_emit_c.sh
// runs through both backends.
// EXPECT-RUNTIME-ERROR: substr start -1 out of bounds (len 5)
fn main() {
    print(substr("hello", -1, 2))
}
